<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mpondomise</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as amaMpondomise</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Mpondomise are a Xhosa-speaking southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nguni">Nguni</a> people of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eastern-cape">Eastern Cape</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a>, living around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tsolo">Tsolo</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qumbu">Qumbu</a>. Their royal genealogy is shared with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mpondo">Mpondo</a>, from whom they separated many generations before written records, and they were respected by neighbouring peoples as rainmakers. Their kingdom lost its independence to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cape-colony">Cape Colony</a> after the revolt of 1880.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mpondomise.jpg" alt="Mpondomise" width="320" height="226" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Archives anon. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Zonnebloem_College_-_Xhosa_graduates_-_Cape_Town_Cape_Colony_1860.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
